# TypeScript ESM

- `type: module`. Use `.js` specifiers in relative imports.
- Keep `strict` TypeScript. Do not add `any` to silence parser or API types.
- Command handlers in `src/cli.ts` stay thin; put logic in `src/parser`, `src/config`, `src/publish`, `src/substack-api`, or `src/browser`.
- Tests are Vitest `*.test.ts` next to the module, or under `src/test/assurance/` for taxonomy suites.
- After TypeScript changes run `npm run verify:agent` (typecheck, test, inspect `examples/basic.md`).
- Do not add Camoufox/optional browser installs to default paths.
